{%- comment -%}
  "You can have this free" note on the product page of anything in the Free
  Gifts collection - today the personalised towel and the lip balms.

  Why it earns its place: the towel product page is the second most visited
  page on the site, 113 of 436 sessions in a 20-day window, second only to the
  home page. It is also the best selling item by units. And until this snippet
  existed it said nothing at all about being free over £25. A quarter of all
  traffic was arriving at exactly the product we give away, and leaving
  without being told how to get it.

  Membership is read from the collection rather than a tag or a hardcoded
  handle list, so it is the same source of truth the cart picker and the
  Shopify discount use. Add a product to Free Gifts and its page starts saying
  so; remove it and the note disappears. Nothing to keep in sync by hand.

  gift_threshold must match cart-gift and the 'Free Gift Over £25' AUTOMATIC
  discount. Three places, one number - change all three together.

  The wording is deliberate on two points:

  "on other items" - Shopify needs £25 of OTHER units before it hands the gift
  over, so a £23 bag plus this £3.95 towel reads as £26.95 and still does not
  qualify. That surprised us in testing; it will surprise shoppers harder.

  "one offer per order" - Shopify will not combine a Buy X Get Y gift with a
  percentage discount code, and the site advertises 15% off a first order in
  the announcement bar. Saying so here costs one line and saves a shopper
  discovering it at checkout.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign gift_threshold = 2500 -%}
{%- assign is_gift = false -%}
{%- for g in collections['free-gifts'].products -%}
  {%- if g.id == product.id -%}
    {%- assign is_gift = true -%}
    {%- break -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}

{%- if is_gift -%}
  <div class="pdp-gift">
    <p class="pdp-gift__head">Free on orders over {{ gift_threshold | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</p>
    <p class="pdp-gift__body">Spend {{ gift_threshold | money_without_trailing_zeros }} on other items and you can pick this as your free gift in your bag. One offer per order, so it cannot be used together with a discount code.</p>
  </div>

  <style>
    .pdp-gift { margin: 2px 0 0; padding: 10px 12px; border: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.10); border-left: 3px solid var(--primary-dark); border-radius: 8px; background: #f6faf6; }
    .pdp-gift__head { margin: 0; font-size: .85rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--primary-dark); }
    .pdp-gift__body { margin: 4px 0 0; font-size: .74rem; line-height: 1.45; opacity: .72; }
  </style>
{%- endif -%}
